@startsalt
' Screen: Promote Capture to Script Modal
' User Stories:
'   - US-511: As a developer, I can promote a flagged capture into a script node
'   - US-512: As a developer, I can choose an existing script and node position (root or child)
'   - US-513: As a developer, I can auto-generate initial expectations from the agent response

{
  <b>Promote to Script</b>                                              [✕]
  ==
  {
    <b>Source Capture:</b> <i>Refund edge case — SLA breach</i>
    ==
    <b>Target Script</b> <i>(required)</i>
    ^Customer Support Script v2                                          ^
    <i>The capture will become a new node in this script's conversation graph.</i>
    --
    <b>Target Node</b> <i>(required)</i>
    ^Node 14: "Handle SLA complaint"                                     ^
    <i>The new node will be attached relative to this node.</i>
    --
    <b>Position</b>
    --
    {
      (X) <b>Child of selected node</b>
          <i>New node branches from Node 14 as a child.</i>
      --
      ( ) <b>Root (new conversation start)</b>
          <i>New node becomes a new root in the script graph.</i>
    }
    ==
    <b>Input Preview</b> <i>(read-only)</i>
    {+
      "My order #ORD-88214 hasn't arrived and it's been 2 weeks. I paid   "
      "for express shipping which was guaranteed in 2 business days.       "
    }
    ==
    <b>Initial Expectations</b>
    --
    {
      [X] <b>Auto-generate from agent response</b>
          <i>Creates expectations from the captured agent response using the default rubric.</i>
      --
      [ ] <b>Start with blank expectations</b>
          <i>No expectations — define manually after promotion.</i>
    }
    ==
    {
      [Cancel] | [Promote to Script]
    }
  }
}
@endsalt
